1
00:00:01,376 --> 00:00:03,545
[FERIO] I figured
something was up.

2
00:00:03,629 --> 00:00:05,172
-[ALL] Huh?
-Puu?

3
00:00:05,797 --> 00:00:06,965
So this entire time,

4
00:00:08,050 --> 00:00:10,427
I've been with
the Legendary Magic Knights.

5
00:00:11,345 --> 00:00:13,680
We really weren't trying
to fool you.

6
00:00:14,306 --> 00:00:15,933
-It's just--
-You still weren't sure

7
00:00:16,016 --> 00:00:18,393
if I was a friend or foe,
so you kept your guard up.

8
00:00:19,728 --> 00:00:20,896
And we're sorry.

9
00:00:21,563 --> 00:00:23,106
Can't fault you there.

10
00:00:23,190 --> 00:00:24,483
[ALL] Huh?

11
00:00:24,566 --> 00:00:27,152
You have quite the task
from what I've gathered.

12
00:00:27,236 --> 00:00:29,029
Better to be wary of strangers.

13
00:00:29,738 --> 00:00:31,323
You're holding the fate
of Princess Emeraude

14
00:00:31,406 --> 00:00:32,282
in your hands.

15
00:00:33,325 --> 00:00:35,118
I think he's safe.

16
00:00:35,827 --> 00:00:37,996
So I'm comfortable
with telling him everything.

17
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:39,206
Mm.

18
00:00:39,289 --> 00:00:40,207
Mm.

19
00:00:43,085 --> 00:00:46,672
[♪ opening theme song playing]

20
00:02:13,759 --> 00:02:15,886
[HIKARU] We were in a place
called Tokyo Tower.

21
00:02:15,969 --> 00:02:19,181
Then, whoosh. The floor melted
and we sank through it.

22
00:02:19,264 --> 00:02:22,100
Which sent us
falling straight into Cefiro!

23
00:02:22,184 --> 00:02:23,935
Then a wizard
named Clef found us

24
00:02:24,019 --> 00:02:26,605
and asked us for one thing.
Our help.

25
00:02:27,356 --> 00:02:30,275
Because he said
only we could save your world.

26
00:02:30,359 --> 00:02:32,402
You met The Guru Clef?

27
00:02:32,486 --> 00:02:34,780
The greatest mage
to ever wield a staff?

28
00:02:34,863 --> 00:02:37,783
Guess that shrimpy old fart
is kind of a celebrity.

29
00:02:37,866 --> 00:02:39,451
It does appear that way.

30
00:02:40,327 --> 00:02:41,870
[FERIO] Do you know
who summoned you here?

31
00:02:42,412 --> 00:02:44,831
[HIKARU] According to Clef,
it was Princess Emeraude.

32
00:02:45,791 --> 00:02:47,000
[FERIO]
And earlier, you mentioned

33
00:02:47,084 --> 00:02:49,878
she was kidnapped
by her priest, Sol Zagato.

34
00:02:49,961 --> 00:02:51,672
[HIKARU] Clef said that too.

35
00:02:52,297 --> 00:02:54,216
Which definitely
explains things.

36
00:02:54,299 --> 00:02:56,218
Most notably,
why our once tranquil world

37
00:02:56,301 --> 00:02:58,011
has become
a stomping ground for monsters,

38
00:02:58,762 --> 00:03:01,431
as well as why we've suffered
a string of disasters.

39
00:03:01,515 --> 00:03:03,266
All right, now it's your turn.

40
00:03:03,809 --> 00:03:06,228
We laid it out to you
and told you who we are.

41
00:03:06,853 --> 00:03:08,480
I think you should do the same.

42
00:03:09,731 --> 00:03:11,900
Let's say Emeraude
and I go way back.

43
00:03:11,983 --> 00:03:13,485
[ALL] Huh?

44
00:03:14,486 --> 00:03:16,738
[FERIO] Never thought
I'd see the legend come to life.

45
00:03:16,822 --> 00:03:19,533
When the sacred
Pillar of Cefiro falls,

46
00:03:19,616 --> 00:03:20,909
a trio from another world

47
00:03:20,992 --> 00:03:22,494
shall awaken
the mighty Rune Gods

48
00:03:22,577 --> 00:03:24,037
and restore peace.

49
00:03:24,121 --> 00:03:27,040
Thus, shall the legend
of the Magic Knights be born.

50
00:03:27,124 --> 00:03:28,083
Oh, right.

51
00:03:28,375 --> 00:03:30,419
Clef did say something
or other about gods.

52
00:03:30,502 --> 00:03:32,671
How we'd need to wake them
to become Magic Knights.

53
00:03:32,754 --> 00:03:34,506
[sighs] Yeah.
We've heard it all,

54
00:03:34,589 --> 00:03:35,507
but what I wanna know is

55
00:03:35,882 --> 00:03:37,801
why these knights
can't just originate here.

56
00:03:37,884 --> 00:03:39,302
Why call us?

57
00:03:39,386 --> 00:03:41,179
Cefiro's got plenty
of tough guys like you

58
00:03:41,263 --> 00:03:42,222
who can fight.

59
00:03:42,597 --> 00:03:45,267
I've also wondered
about that little detail.

60
00:03:45,350 --> 00:03:48,145
Since a magic knight
needs escudo ore,

61
00:03:48,228 --> 00:03:49,521
I set out for Eterna

62
00:03:49,604 --> 00:03:51,773
to see if I could fulfill
the legend myself.

63
00:03:52,566 --> 00:03:54,609
I have no idea
where Princess Emeraude is

64
00:03:54,693 --> 00:03:56,862
or what condition she may be in,

65
00:03:56,945 --> 00:03:59,156
but it's clear
her prayers have stopped,

66
00:03:59,239 --> 00:04:01,616
as if her heart is too troubled
to wish for peace.

67
00:04:03,243 --> 00:04:06,079
So the skies rage
and the land roars.

68
00:04:06,872 --> 00:04:09,583
People have grown anxious,
even terrified,

69
00:04:09,666 --> 00:04:12,794
and their destructive feelings
create devastating monsters.

70
00:04:12,878 --> 00:04:15,422
You mean the things we fought?

71
00:04:17,841 --> 00:04:19,968
[FERIO] They were
negative emotions made flesh.

72
00:04:20,969 --> 00:04:23,138
When everyone's scared
and worried sick,

73
00:04:23,638 --> 00:04:25,223
their fears create monsters.

74
00:04:25,307 --> 00:04:28,810
Since the force of will
can bring about paradise,

75
00:04:28,894 --> 00:04:31,813
it's natural that
it could also invite disaster.

76
00:04:32,439 --> 00:04:35,734
Cefiro.
What a wacky world to call home.

77
00:04:36,485 --> 00:04:38,570
It's a far cry from home now.

78
00:04:38,653 --> 00:04:40,989
As Cefiro began plunging
into chaos,

79
00:04:41,072 --> 00:04:42,657
many of our finest realized

80
00:04:42,741 --> 00:04:45,076
something must have happened
to the princess,

81
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:46,328
and made for her castle.

82
00:04:47,287 --> 00:04:49,289
Sadly, none of those
courageous souls

83
00:04:49,372 --> 00:04:50,373
were ever seen again.

84
00:04:51,374 --> 00:04:53,793
Makes sense
if they clashed with Sol Zagato.

85
00:04:53,877 --> 00:04:55,045
Never stood a chance.

86
00:04:55,128 --> 00:04:57,923
Come on.
Not like he's invincible.

87
00:04:58,006 --> 00:04:59,883
He might as well be.

88
00:04:59,966 --> 00:05:02,177
I think I can feel
my resolve slipping away!

89
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:05,514
You said these people
were Cefiro's finest.

90
00:05:05,597 --> 00:05:06,973
Were they all like you?

91
00:05:07,057 --> 00:05:09,434
Trying to become
Magic Knights on their own?

92
00:05:11,520 --> 00:05:12,562
Not one.

93
00:05:12,646 --> 00:05:14,689
Only those close
to Princess Emeraude

94
00:05:14,773 --> 00:05:16,316
even know the legend.

95
00:05:16,399 --> 00:05:18,443
And that is a very select group.

96
00:05:18,527 --> 00:05:21,196
Oh, but you knew it.

97
00:05:21,279 --> 00:05:23,740
[laughs awkwardly]

98
00:05:24,407 --> 00:05:25,992
-[FERIO] Anyway.
-Huh?

99
00:05:26,076 --> 00:05:28,245
If Princess Emeraude
did in fact summon

100
00:05:28,328 --> 00:05:29,538
the three of you here,

101
00:05:30,205 --> 00:05:31,331
then I'm out of luck,

102
00:05:31,790 --> 00:05:33,667
because it seems
Magic Knights do have to come

103
00:05:33,750 --> 00:05:34,668
from another world.

104
00:05:37,879 --> 00:05:38,880
-[BOTH] Huh?
-It's doing

105
00:05:38,964 --> 00:05:40,465
the red glowy-thing again.

106
00:05:43,134 --> 00:05:45,512
I guess the Spring of Eterna
is that way.

107
00:05:47,389 --> 00:05:49,349
-[gasps]
-Ferio?

108
00:05:49,432 --> 00:05:52,477
I said I would guard you
until we got out of the forest.

109
00:05:53,103 --> 00:05:54,229
[whimpers]

110
00:06:00,443 --> 00:06:01,820
What's this?

111
00:06:02,654 --> 00:06:03,655
It's for you.

112
00:06:04,990 --> 00:06:07,826
Oh, but I have nothing
I can offer you in exchange.

113
00:06:07,909 --> 00:06:10,829
♪

114
00:06:10,912 --> 00:06:12,080
[gasps]

115
00:06:12,706 --> 00:06:14,082
Buy her dinner first!

116
00:06:14,165 --> 00:06:16,334
That was a good exchange to me.

117
00:06:17,210 --> 00:06:18,795
[gasps]

118
00:06:18,878 --> 00:06:21,214
We'll meet again soon enough.

119
00:06:21,298 --> 00:06:23,049
Take care of yourselves,
Magic Knights.

120
00:06:26,887 --> 00:06:30,682
What's his deal?
Like, that was way too smooth.

121
00:06:30,765 --> 00:06:34,144
Did he activate his prince mode?
Are you okay?

122
00:06:34,227 --> 00:06:36,855
-Ground control to Fuu!
-[gasps]

123
00:06:36,938 --> 00:06:39,858
Yes, I was listening,
and everything's perfectly fine!

124
00:06:39,941 --> 00:06:41,568
You're redder than a lobster.

125
00:06:41,651 --> 00:06:43,153
I, um, what?

126
00:06:43,236 --> 00:06:45,447
Please, you know what.

127
00:06:45,530 --> 00:06:46,740
Puu, puu!

128
00:06:46,823 --> 00:06:48,742
Um, Mokona wants us to head out.

129
00:06:48,825 --> 00:06:50,619
Right! Good call! Ready?

130
00:06:50,702 --> 00:06:52,704
-Forward march!
-[groans]

131
00:06:52,787 --> 00:06:54,706
You're marching off
the wrong way.

132
00:06:54,789 --> 00:06:56,416
[Alcyone groaning]

133
00:06:57,208 --> 00:06:58,501
Lord Zagato.

134
00:06:59,336 --> 00:07:01,046
I almost had them.

135
00:07:01,963 --> 00:07:05,175
But again, I failed you.

136
00:07:06,051 --> 00:07:07,469
Forgive me.

137
00:07:08,094 --> 00:07:10,263
The power
Magic Knights can wield,

138
00:07:10,347 --> 00:07:11,681
it's devastating.

139
00:07:11,765 --> 00:07:15,101
But I swear,
I will aid your cause.

140
00:07:15,810 --> 00:07:17,312
I will obey your every command!

141
00:07:17,395 --> 00:07:19,147
♪

142
00:07:19,814 --> 00:07:21,650
Your desires are my own!

143
00:07:22,692 --> 00:07:25,278
My beloved Lord Zagato.

144
00:07:25,362 --> 00:07:26,863
Then die.

145
00:07:26,947 --> 00:07:27,822
[gasps]

146
00:07:29,199 --> 00:07:32,285
[Alcyone screaming]

147
00:07:33,411 --> 00:07:35,997
No, please! Have mercy!

148
00:07:36,581 --> 00:07:39,042
Spare me, my love!

149
00:07:42,837 --> 00:07:45,715
[woman laughs] Pathetic.

150
00:07:45,799 --> 00:07:47,634
[BOY] She lost to them twice,

151
00:07:47,717 --> 00:07:49,969
then made an even bigger fool
of herself here.

152
00:07:50,053 --> 00:07:53,682
[MAN] Yet those brats
are making the legend a reality.

153
00:07:53,765 --> 00:07:56,893
Perhaps they shall save
Cefiro after all.

154
00:07:56,976 --> 00:07:58,853
[BOY] Nah, we've just started.

155
00:07:58,937 --> 00:08:00,689
So, with your permission,

156
00:08:00,772 --> 00:08:03,274
I'd like a crack at them,
Zagato.

157
00:08:03,358 --> 00:08:05,777
[scoffs] Very well.

158
00:08:05,860 --> 00:08:08,071
Your turn, Ascot.

159
00:08:08,154 --> 00:08:10,782
[giggles] With pleasure. Bye!

160
00:08:12,158 --> 00:08:13,368
[birds squawking]

161
00:08:13,451 --> 00:08:14,452
-[grunts]
-[sword slashes]

162
00:08:15,704 --> 00:08:16,705
-[grunts]
-[flower monster growls]

163
00:08:16,788 --> 00:08:18,540
[grunts]

164
00:08:19,416 --> 00:08:20,458
[growls]

165
00:08:20,542 --> 00:08:22,752
[grunts]

166
00:08:26,506 --> 00:08:28,633
Can people really worry
a plant monster

167
00:08:28,717 --> 00:08:30,385
into existence here?

168
00:08:30,468 --> 00:08:33,221
It felt real enough
when I cut it in half.

169
00:08:33,304 --> 00:08:36,141
[FUU] How many more stand
between us and Eterna?

170
00:08:36,224 --> 00:08:37,809
Puu, puu!

171
00:08:38,435 --> 00:08:40,061
Mokona says it's just up ahead.

172
00:08:40,145 --> 00:08:42,021
[all panting]

173
00:08:42,105 --> 00:08:43,773
-[gasps]
-Huh?

174
00:08:46,651 --> 00:08:47,819
So, like,

175
00:08:47,902 --> 00:08:50,280
could one of you
please point out the spring?

176
00:08:50,363 --> 00:08:52,574
The name did lead me
to think there'd be water.

177
00:08:53,450 --> 00:08:54,826
Puu, puu!

178
00:08:54,909 --> 00:08:56,703
-[groans]
-Mokona!

179
00:08:57,328 --> 00:08:58,830
I can admit,
you were a crucial part

180
00:08:58,913 --> 00:09:00,540
in schooling Madame Doom again.

181
00:09:00,623 --> 00:09:02,542
I got my magic 101 lesson
from Clef

182
00:09:02,625 --> 00:09:03,960
thanks to your telepathy.

183
00:09:04,043 --> 00:09:05,086
But now,

184
00:09:05,170 --> 00:09:06,671
you've screwed things up
majorly!

185
00:09:06,755 --> 00:09:07,839
-[Mokona giggling]
-You were supposed...

186
00:09:07,922 --> 00:09:10,717
-She's scary. And loud.
-[Fuu giggles]

187
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:12,051
[UMI] What are we doing
in the middle

188
00:09:12,135 --> 00:09:13,386
of some random field?

189
00:09:13,470 --> 00:09:15,054
We're looking for
weapon materials,

190
00:09:15,138 --> 00:09:16,639
not a place to eat lunch!

191
00:09:16,723 --> 00:09:18,099
You're right.

192
00:09:18,183 --> 00:09:19,517
This plateau here would make

193
00:09:19,601 --> 00:09:22,061
for a lovely spot
to enjoy lunch outdoors.

194
00:09:22,145 --> 00:09:23,646
-Wait.
-Huh?

195
00:09:23,730 --> 00:09:26,316
-What's that?
-[FUU] What's what, Miss Hikaru?

196
00:09:26,399 --> 00:09:29,068
-The plateau?
-The line floating above it.

197
00:09:29,152 --> 00:09:30,069
A line?

198
00:09:30,779 --> 00:09:31,654
Hmm?

199
00:09:32,906 --> 00:09:33,823
[Umi groans]

200
00:09:35,492 --> 00:09:36,951
There is, indeed, a line.

201
00:09:37,035 --> 00:09:39,287
But what for?

202
00:09:39,370 --> 00:09:41,080
I don't have a clue.

203
00:09:41,164 --> 00:09:43,333
Sometimes, there's just
a weird line in the air.

204
00:09:43,958 --> 00:09:45,460
I can't accept pointless

205
00:09:45,543 --> 00:09:47,212
-floating horizontal lines!
-[MOKONA] Puu!

206
00:09:47,295 --> 00:09:48,713
-[FUU] Cefiro is a very...
-[Hikaru gasps] Mokona!

207
00:09:48,797 --> 00:09:49,756
...mysterious place.

208
00:09:49,839 --> 00:09:51,549
[UMI] And the biggest mystery

209
00:09:51,633 --> 00:09:54,052
might be finding
this legendary spring!

210
00:09:54,135 --> 00:09:55,178
-[HIKARU] Whoa!
-[BOTH] Huh?

211
00:09:55,261 --> 00:09:56,888
[UMI] What are you on about?

212
00:09:56,971 --> 00:09:59,182
[HIKARU]
You gotta get up here. Quick!

213
00:09:59,265 --> 00:10:00,600
♪

214
00:10:01,351 --> 00:10:03,436
-Look down.
-[both gasp]

215
00:10:04,145 --> 00:10:05,647
[UMI] Is that the spring?!

216
00:10:05,730 --> 00:10:07,482
[FUU] Which means
our biggest mystery

217
00:10:07,565 --> 00:10:08,483
was just solved.

218
00:10:08,817 --> 00:10:11,486
How?! It wasn't there
a second ago, right?

219
00:10:14,948 --> 00:10:16,324
No, it sure was.

220
00:10:16,407 --> 00:10:17,575
[BOTH] Huh?

221
00:10:17,659 --> 00:10:18,993
It's the line.

222
00:10:19,285 --> 00:10:21,996
You just can't see it clearly
until you change your view.

223
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:24,749
Yes, of course. It's flat.

224
00:10:24,833 --> 00:10:27,502
This is my first time
seeing a 2D spring.

225
00:10:27,585 --> 00:10:28,962
[Mokona giggles]

226
00:10:29,045 --> 00:10:31,422
-[both grunt]
-Well, there's the spring,

227
00:10:31,506 --> 00:10:33,258
so where's all the escudo ore?

228
00:10:33,716 --> 00:10:36,135
None of these rocks
strike me as legendary.

229
00:10:37,053 --> 00:10:38,304
-Hmm.
-Puu!

230
00:10:38,388 --> 00:10:40,640
-Maybe the ore's inside?
-[giggles]

231
00:10:40,723 --> 00:10:42,392
What?!

232
00:10:42,475 --> 00:10:45,186
[groans] I really miss logic.

233
00:10:45,270 --> 00:10:48,147
Cefiro is more of a land
of wonders than logic, though.

234
00:10:48,231 --> 00:10:49,190
[chuckles nervously]

235
00:10:49,274 --> 00:10:51,651
These wonders should chill out!

236
00:10:51,734 --> 00:10:53,444
Hey! Careful!

237
00:10:53,528 --> 00:10:54,904
Puu-uu!

238
00:10:54,988 --> 00:10:56,114
Mokona!

239
00:10:56,197 --> 00:10:59,325
-[UMI] No more fluffball.
-[gasps]

240
00:10:59,409 --> 00:11:00,535
Mokona.

241
00:11:00,618 --> 00:11:01,995
[water bubbling]

242
00:11:02,078 --> 00:11:03,371
-[whimpering]
-[FUU] It seems

243
00:11:03,454 --> 00:11:06,332
if you want to proceed,
we have to jump in.

244
00:11:06,416 --> 00:11:08,543
But how deep does the water go?

245
00:11:08,626 --> 00:11:09,711
And can we even breathe

246
00:11:09,794 --> 00:11:10,753
-inside there?
-Mokona!

247
00:11:11,296 --> 00:11:14,424
Well, let's take a leap of faith
and find your answers.

248
00:11:14,507 --> 00:11:17,844
[sighs] The craziness
just won't let up at all!

249
00:11:17,927 --> 00:11:19,596
-[HIKARU] I say we go.
-[BOTH] Huh?

250
00:11:20,263 --> 00:11:21,848
It's the only way forward.

251
00:11:22,265 --> 00:11:23,474
Mokona jumped in the spring

252
00:11:23,558 --> 00:11:25,852
to tell us that's where
we can find escudo ore.

253
00:11:27,103 --> 00:11:29,188
We decided we'd become
Magic Knights,

254
00:11:30,106 --> 00:11:31,608
and we can't do it
without the ore.

255
00:11:32,483 --> 00:11:34,777
-Touché.
-Let's go.

256
00:11:34,861 --> 00:11:37,238
What comes next
is anyone's guess,

257
00:11:37,322 --> 00:11:39,741
but I know
I'd rather face it together.

258
00:11:39,824 --> 00:11:42,243
'Cause three Magic Knights
are better than one!

259
00:11:42,327 --> 00:11:44,245
Hands down!

260
00:11:44,329 --> 00:11:47,165
♪

261
00:11:49,792 --> 00:11:52,879
Here goes nothing!

262
00:11:54,422 --> 00:11:55,757
[water splashes]

263
00:12:07,185 --> 00:12:08,144
[groans]

264
00:12:08,937 --> 00:12:12,190
[gasps] Fuu! Umi! Where are you?

265
00:12:14,525 --> 00:12:16,402
[grunts]

266
00:12:17,445 --> 00:12:18,404
A monster?

267
00:12:20,907 --> 00:12:22,200
[gasps]

268
00:12:22,283 --> 00:12:25,328
Hikari. But how?

269
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:30,333
Hikaru? Fuu? Where did you go?

270
00:12:31,084 --> 00:12:32,669
♪

271
00:12:32,752 --> 00:12:34,837
[grunts, gasps]

272
00:12:36,839 --> 00:12:40,885
-[both chuckle]
-Mom? Dad? Is that you?

273
00:12:41,844 --> 00:12:44,639
Huh? Looks like
we can breathe down here.

274
00:12:44,722 --> 00:12:46,683
-[footsteps approaching]
-[gasps]

275
00:12:46,766 --> 00:12:47,976
[grunts]

276
00:12:50,895 --> 00:12:51,854
[gasps]

277
00:12:53,564 --> 00:12:54,440
Me?

278
00:12:56,067 --> 00:12:56,943
[HIKARU] Hey, boy.

279
00:12:57,902 --> 00:13:00,822
How'd you wind up here
of all places?

280
00:13:00,905 --> 00:13:02,907
[gasps] Hikari!

281
00:13:03,533 --> 00:13:04,909
What's gotten into you?

282
00:13:05,535 --> 00:13:07,453
[growling]

283
00:13:09,163 --> 00:13:11,207
[screams]

284
00:13:11,290 --> 00:13:14,711
Stop! It's me! Hikaru!

285
00:13:14,794 --> 00:13:16,921
Can't you tell it's me?

286
00:13:17,005 --> 00:13:18,172
[grunts]

287
00:13:23,136 --> 00:13:24,762
[gasps]

288
00:13:25,555 --> 00:13:26,723
What's wrong?

289
00:13:28,057 --> 00:13:30,810
[UMI] If you're here right now,
this must be a dream.

290
00:13:31,269 --> 00:13:32,603
It has to be.

291
00:13:34,063 --> 00:13:37,859
I'm in Cefiro,
in the Spring of Eterna.

292
00:13:38,776 --> 00:13:41,446
Cefiro!
Maybe that was the dream!

293
00:13:41,529 --> 00:13:43,823
-All along!
-[both chuckle]

294
00:13:45,908 --> 00:13:47,952
[Umi screams]

295
00:13:48,411 --> 00:13:50,038
[groans, gasps]

296
00:13:50,830 --> 00:13:53,791
Dream or not, that pain is real.

297
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:59,255
Just checking.
But you’re not a mirror, right?

298
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:04,177
[gasps]

299
00:14:07,805 --> 00:14:09,599
Guess Umi had a point.

300
00:14:10,141 --> 00:14:11,684
The craziness won't let up.

301
00:14:14,687 --> 00:14:17,857
[exclaims, gasps]

302
00:14:18,524 --> 00:14:22,111
My arrow struck her shoulder,
didn't it?

303
00:14:24,989 --> 00:14:26,866
[screams, grunts]

304
00:14:27,325 --> 00:14:29,660
[groans, gasps]

305
00:14:30,870 --> 00:14:33,831
If one of us gets hurt,
so does the other.

306
00:14:34,248 --> 00:14:37,502
She's not some doppelganger.
She's me!

307
00:14:39,545 --> 00:14:40,755
[grunts, gasps]

308
00:14:41,464 --> 00:14:43,591
I don't wanna fight you!
I won't!

309
00:14:43,674 --> 00:14:46,344
We've been together
for all our lives.

310
00:14:47,220 --> 00:14:49,931
You were there when I smiled
and laughed on good days,

311
00:14:50,014 --> 00:14:52,058
and when I cried on bad ones.

312
00:14:52,141 --> 00:14:53,226
♪

313
00:14:53,309 --> 00:14:56,270
[sniffles]
I love you so much, Hikari.

314
00:14:56,354 --> 00:14:58,231
I tell you all the time!

315
00:14:58,314 --> 00:14:59,649
So why?

316
00:15:00,316 --> 00:15:02,235
What happened? [gasps]

317
00:15:02,318 --> 00:15:03,986
-[slashes]
-[Hikari yelps]

318
00:15:04,070 --> 00:15:04,946
[gasps]

319
00:15:05,696 --> 00:15:07,532
I'm sorry! [yells]

320
00:15:07,615 --> 00:15:09,492
[choking]

321
00:15:10,827 --> 00:15:11,744
Why?

322
00:15:13,079 --> 00:15:14,497
Are you acting this way

323
00:15:15,248 --> 00:15:16,833
because you don't
love me anymore?

324
00:15:16,916 --> 00:15:18,251
[Umi screams]

325
00:15:18,334 --> 00:15:21,963
All right! Enough! Enough!

326
00:15:23,798 --> 00:15:27,593
Dragon of Water! [gasps]

327
00:15:30,304 --> 00:15:32,640
Oh, no! It hit!

328
00:15:37,812 --> 00:15:39,147
-[both grunt]
-[Umi screams]

329
00:15:39,856 --> 00:15:41,315
[groans] It's no use!

330
00:15:44,694 --> 00:15:47,280
I can't bring myself
to fight my parents.

331
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:49,031
I just can't.

332
00:15:49,866 --> 00:15:53,119
[FUU] If I attack,
I damage myself in the process,

333
00:15:53,578 --> 00:15:55,288
and if she lands
an attack on me,

334
00:15:55,371 --> 00:15:57,248
I obviously get damaged too.

335
00:15:57,748 --> 00:15:59,041
It's a lose-lose.

336
00:16:00,042 --> 00:16:03,254
What's more,
she's not the least bit winded.

337
00:16:03,337 --> 00:16:04,505
[gasps]

338
00:16:05,047 --> 00:16:07,049
[gasps]

339
00:16:07,133 --> 00:16:08,259
[gasps]

340
00:16:13,681 --> 00:16:15,433
[EMERAUDE] O, Magic Knights.

341
00:16:15,516 --> 00:16:17,059
[all gasp]

342
00:16:17,143 --> 00:16:18,144
Hang on!

343
00:16:18,227 --> 00:16:19,395
That voice.

344
00:16:19,479 --> 00:16:22,023
Who's there? Hello?

345
00:16:23,024 --> 00:16:25,818
[EMERAUDE]
Brave young girls from afar.

346
00:16:26,486 --> 00:16:29,530
[HIKARU] I heard you before.
At Tokyo Tower!

347
00:16:30,406 --> 00:16:31,574
It was you.

348
00:16:31,657 --> 00:16:34,035
The one who summoned us
to Cefiro was you.

349
00:16:34,118 --> 00:16:36,078
Princess Emeraude.

350
00:16:36,787 --> 00:16:39,248
Indeed, I am Emeraude of Cefiro.

351
00:16:40,291 --> 00:16:42,251
Take courage, Magic Knights.

352
00:16:42,335 --> 00:16:45,421
Do not allow sorrow
to extinguish the light within.

353
00:16:46,923 --> 00:16:50,343
You must be
of strong heart and sound mind.

354
00:16:51,302 --> 00:16:54,347
Now,
who is the adversary you face?

355
00:16:55,097 --> 00:16:57,558
Is it someone
you would deem irreplaceable?

356
00:16:57,642 --> 00:16:59,560
Yes! Hikari's precious!

357
00:16:59,644 --> 00:17:02,813
He stays when I cry,
and he worries when I fall.

358
00:17:03,397 --> 00:17:06,067
He's the very best friend
that I've ever had.

359
00:17:06,692 --> 00:17:08,903
He may not communicate
with words,

360
00:17:08,986 --> 00:17:10,112
but we don't need them

361
00:17:10,196 --> 00:17:12,114
since we understand
each other's hearts!

362
00:17:12,198 --> 00:17:13,741
Irreplaceable?

363
00:17:13,824 --> 00:17:17,119
I'm facing my mom and dad!
The people I love most!

364
00:17:17,203 --> 00:17:19,830
So much that once I grow up,
I want to repay them

365
00:17:19,914 --> 00:17:21,457
for all they put
into raising me!

366
00:17:21,541 --> 00:17:22,875
Monetarily, sure.

367
00:17:22,959 --> 00:17:26,629
But I... I mainly want
to repay the love they gave.

368
00:17:26,712 --> 00:17:30,007
I'll store it all,
each memory and kind gesture.

369
00:17:30,091 --> 00:17:32,343
Then I'll return it, bit by bit!

370
00:17:32,426 --> 00:17:35,137
Very much!
Because I'm facing myself.

371
00:17:35,805 --> 00:17:37,723
So of course I'm irreplaceable.

372
00:17:37,807 --> 00:17:39,767
My parents and sister
all love me.

373
00:17:40,560 --> 00:17:42,937
They would be crushed
if the worst came to pass,

374
00:17:43,020 --> 00:17:44,939
so I live
as best I can for them!

375
00:17:45,690 --> 00:17:47,316
I'm still a child, though.

376
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:49,902
At my age,
I can't really do a whole lot.

377
00:17:50,528 --> 00:17:53,781
But I try.
As small as it may seem,

378
00:17:53,864 --> 00:17:56,409
I stay happy
so those I love will too!

379
00:17:57,660 --> 00:18:00,955
That's why I treasure
my life with all I have!

380
00:18:01,038 --> 00:18:03,124
Your hearts
are in the right place.

381
00:18:03,207 --> 00:18:05,418
Now, take a moment
to really think.

382
00:18:05,501 --> 00:18:08,379
Would the ones you cherish
ever mean to hurt you?

383
00:18:08,462 --> 00:18:09,672
[all gasp]

384
00:18:09,755 --> 00:18:11,632
Would they wish
to see you suffer?

385
00:18:11,716 --> 00:18:14,176
Or cause you to cry out in pain?

386
00:18:14,802 --> 00:18:16,137
You know the answer.

387
00:18:16,887 --> 00:18:21,392
Trust it. Then,
claim your prize. The escudo.

388
00:18:24,645 --> 00:18:25,813
She's gone.

389
00:18:28,232 --> 00:18:30,735
[HIKARU] No.
Hikari wouldn't do this!

390
00:18:31,986 --> 00:18:34,780
He's a good boy
who's gentle and protects me.

391
00:18:35,448 --> 00:18:36,991
[grunts]

392
00:18:37,074 --> 00:18:38,326
♪

393
00:18:38,409 --> 00:18:39,785
You're just a big fake!

394
00:18:39,869 --> 00:18:41,454
[UMI] What was I thinking?

395
00:18:41,537 --> 00:18:44,081
Mom and Dad wouldn't blast me
with shock waves!

396
00:18:45,041 --> 00:18:46,959
[grunts] It's fine!

397
00:18:47,418 --> 00:18:49,920
My magic will heal
these wounds later.

398
00:18:50,004 --> 00:18:52,423
How dare you use Hikari
against me?

399
00:18:52,506 --> 00:18:55,092
My home's too happy
for this melodrama!

400
00:18:55,176 --> 00:18:57,053
It would shatter
my family's hearts

401
00:18:57,136 --> 00:18:59,138
if I were hurt beyond hope!

402
00:19:00,681 --> 00:19:05,019
[HIKARU] Crimson Lightning!

403
00:19:05,102 --> 00:19:08,439
Aqua Tornado!

404
00:19:08,522 --> 00:19:10,566
Emerald Gale!

405
00:19:10,649 --> 00:19:11,734
[Hikari yelps]

406
00:19:11,817 --> 00:19:13,444
-[both groan]
-[Fuu groans]

407
00:19:15,154 --> 00:19:16,447
[gasps]

408
00:19:23,245 --> 00:19:24,497
What do you know?

409
00:19:25,081 --> 00:19:26,040
Oh, my.

410
00:19:26,332 --> 00:19:29,502
[gasps] This thing's
gotta be escudo ore.

411
00:19:35,508 --> 00:19:36,384
[gasps]

412
00:19:36,467 --> 00:19:37,635
[Umi gasps]

413
00:19:37,718 --> 00:19:38,761
[gasps]

414
00:19:42,348 --> 00:19:44,308
The armor from Clef transformed.

415
00:19:44,392 --> 00:19:48,062
It looks way fancier.
Not to mention, good as new.

416
00:19:48,145 --> 00:19:49,855
A self-upgrade?

417
00:19:49,939 --> 00:19:52,983
Did something else upgrade too?
Huh?

418
00:19:53,067 --> 00:19:54,443
[gasping]

419
00:19:54,527 --> 00:19:56,696
[groaning]

420
00:20:06,288 --> 00:20:08,207
[groans]

421
00:20:08,290 --> 00:20:10,459
-What the--
-[ALL] Huh?

422
00:20:11,794 --> 00:20:13,754
We're floating!
Like, in the air!

423
00:20:13,838 --> 00:20:16,549
[PRESEA] No need
to make such a fuss.

424
00:20:16,632 --> 00:20:17,842
[ALL] Uh.

425
00:20:18,467 --> 00:20:21,762
Floating over Eterna like that
can only mean one thing.

426
00:20:21,846 --> 00:20:24,473
You found the escudo.
Quickly too.

427
00:20:24,557 --> 00:20:26,183
[HIKARU] Presea!

428
00:20:26,267 --> 00:20:28,060
Wait! Where'd it go?

429
00:20:28,144 --> 00:20:30,062
Try looking above your heads.

430
00:20:30,146 --> 00:20:31,272
[ALL] Huh?

431
00:20:33,899 --> 00:20:36,444
Now, come forth, girls.

432
00:20:36,527 --> 00:20:39,155
As the highest ranked Pharl
in all of Cefiro,

433
00:20:39,238 --> 00:20:41,949
I, Presea,
shall take the ore you found

434
00:20:42,032 --> 00:20:43,993
and forge it
into the finest blades

435
00:20:44,076 --> 00:20:45,578
you've ever laid eyes on.

436
00:20:46,245 --> 00:20:48,789
Weapons worthy
of the title you bear.

437
00:20:50,124 --> 00:20:51,041
[all grunt]

438
00:20:52,543 --> 00:20:54,044
♪

439
00:21:09,560 --> 00:21:11,937
Oh, wow. She's stunning.

440
00:21:14,523 --> 00:21:17,735
Pretty, but it's not
what I thought she'd do.

441
00:21:17,818 --> 00:21:19,862
It's both strange
and enchanting.

442
00:21:22,323 --> 00:21:23,741
They're all swords.

443
00:21:24,241 --> 00:21:25,159
[PRESEA] Yes.

444
00:21:25,242 --> 00:21:27,286
The arms of the Magic Knights.

445
00:21:30,456 --> 00:21:31,874
One-of-a-kind weapons

446
00:21:31,957 --> 00:21:34,668
I fashioned for you
and you alone.

447
00:21:34,752 --> 00:21:36,754
No one else can wield them.

448
00:21:39,006 --> 00:21:40,966
[♪ closing theme song playing]

